I left out the `last-input` write. The node's `with` clause grants only `http-client`, `notifier`, and `wall-clock`. A store write would need a `state-rw` import, which would extend the node's authority beyond that clause. Recording the input would need a separate grant. The output is unchanged by this omission.

The `ensures notified == true` contract also rules out returning `notified: false`, so if the notifier refuses, the body traps instead of producing a non-conforming output.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, notifier};
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        // Read the clock once; this is the only time source the node has.
        let now = wall_clock::now();

        // The one permitted fetch. A host outside the allowlist traps at the
        // boundary; a transport failure also traps here, since the report has
        // no error case to carry it.
        let body = http_client::get(&feed_url);

        // Report how many characters came back. The body is untrusted, so it is
        // counted and never echoed into the notification or the report.
        let fetched = u32::try_from(body.chars().count()).unwrap_or(u32::MAX);

        let message = format!(
            "heartbeat: {} chars from {} at {}",
            fetched, feed_url, now.seconds
        );

        // The ensures clause requires notified == true for every output, so a
        // refused notification must not produce a report. Trap instead.
        if !notifier::notify(&message) {
            panic!("notifier refused the heartbeat; ensures notified == true cannot hold");
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds: now.seconds,
            fetched,
            notified: true,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

